            "footnote_ref": null,
            "href": null,
            "math": null,
            "styles": [],
            "text": "Tides in the inner harbor follow a semidiurnal pattern with two highs and two lows each lunar day. The range at the north wall averages two point one meters, and spring tides add roughly forty centimeters to that figure. Gauges were read every ten minutes for a full year."
          }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
      },
      {
        "attrs": {},
        "id": "b0004",
        "parent_id": null,
        "provenance": {
